  "required_invariants": [
    "For a complete physical bolt line, the line resultant is the vector sum of the actual Stage 2.5A total bolt-demand vectors on that line.",
    "Eccentric shear-out handoff is authorized only when the line resultant is exactly parallel and nonnegative in the canonical connection-force direction.",
    "A zero line resultant does not require a shear-out demand comparison.",
    "A reversed or nonparallel line resultant is fail-closed in RC1.",
    "The existing Stage 2.4B shear-out resistance equation and factors are not changed.",
    "Pitch, e1, row span, and geometry come from accepted canonical plans and are not re-derived from demand.",
    "For nonzero residual moment, general first-row net-tension handoff remains unsupported because the source model assumes bearing and bypass loads aligned with the connection force and equal bolt sharing within a row.",
    "A zero-residual case reproduces the existing Stage 2.4B first-row and shear-out behavior exactly.",
    "Known supported shear-out failure remains FAIL even while first-row net tension remains unsupported.",
    "Supported shear-out PASS plus unsupported first-row net tension never becomes ordinary PASS.",
